<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The platform theme, which does almost nothing.

      Colours, typography and surfaces come from Compose
      (`ui/theme/Theme.kt`), including the dynamic-colour path on Android 12+.
      What is left for XML is the window itself, and the one thing that must be
      right before the first Compose frame: the background, so a launch on a
      light device does not flash dark.

      Note what is NOT here: `windowLightStatusBar` and `windowLightNavigationBar`.
      Those are set programmatically by `enableEdgeToEdge()` in `MainActivity`,
      which picks the right icon tint from the theme and does it correctly across
      API levels. Declaring them here as well would be a second source of truth
      for the same fact — and `windowLightNavigationBar` needs API 27 while this
      app supports 26, so the XML copy would also be wrong on the oldest
      supported devices.

      The parent is the platform Material theme rather than AppCompat, so the app
      carries no AppCompat dependency at all.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.TailnetByok" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#F6F8FB</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <!--
          FLAG_SECURE is intentionally NOT set. It would block screenshots of the
          connection test — which is the main thing a user needs to share when
          asking for help — and the only secret on screen is masked behind a
          password field. If you disagree, this is the one-line place to change
          it, and docs/SECURITY-MODEL.md records the reasoning.
        -->
    </style>
</resources>
